# Security

- Never hardcode API keys, OAuth secrets, or tokens in source code
- Webhook payloads: verify signatures (HMAC-SHA256) before processing
- Parameterized queries only — watch raw SQL for string formatting with external input
- Rate limit user-facing API endpoints (`frappe.rate_limiter.rate_limit`)
- Every `@frappe.whitelist()` endpoint must have a role-based access check — "security through obscurity" is not security
- OAuth tokens: handle refresh gracefully, never expose refresh_token to frontend
- Log message IDs only — never log full message content or PII
- Sanitize user input before storage (`frappe.utils.sanitize_html` for HTML content)
- CORS: whitelist specific origins in production
